## Read before any ticket
1. `.ops/memory/DECISIONS.md` — decisions are binding; do not re-decide.
2. The ticket file under `.ops/tickets/` — scope, AC, gate commands.
3. Only the skills listed in the ticket's `skills:` frontmatter.

## Ticket type → skills
| Ticket touches | Load |
|---|---|
| DB, repositories, tools with scope | `<p>-tenancy-rules`, `drizzle-orm-patterns` |
| API routes / plugins | `fastify-best-practices`, `<p>-tenancy-rules` |
| Metrics / money | `<p>-domain-math`, `vitest` |
| Agents / tools | `<p>-agent-platform` |
| UI | `<p>-ux-principles`, `web-design-guidelines`, `nextjs-app-router-patterns` |
| Tests only | `vitest` (+ `playwright-best-practices` for E2E) |
| `.ops/` files | `<p>-ops-logging` |

## Hard rules
- Every tenant-owned table/query/tool carries workspace + tenant scope; never trust an ID
  supplied by a model or a URL as authorization.
- No placeholders, `TODO`, stubbed returns or skipped tests in delivered code.
- No new dependencies without a note in "Implementer notes".
- Do not commit. Do not expand scope. Leave findings under "Implementer notes".
- Diff stays under ~400 changed lines; if it can't, stop and say so.
- Conventions: <link docs/conventions/>. Errors use typed codes; money is integer minor units;
  timestamps UTC; business periods in tenant timezone.

## Report contract (end of every run)
Summary · files changed · gates run with output tail · open questions · decisions you made.
